Aerie-Purpose: Let an auto-hidden sidebar float over the page without taking room, give the rail its fixed 56 px and no resizer, and open an auto-hidden sidebar on F6.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui/views/frame (vertical_tab_strip_region_view.cc/.h, layout/browser_view_tabbed_layout_impl.cc, BUILD.gn)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #184. The region view stays visible when the density is auto-hide and the sidebar is undocked, with no flow width; the layout
gives it the width in the kFloatingWidth property as expand-on-hover style overlap. The rail has min width 56 and no resize area; a
density change re-reads the width. A resize tells the sidebar view, so that the peek holds the sidebar open while it runs.

